{{Quote|Seek out the Warframe Mirage|Quest Description}}'''Hidden Messages''' is a side [[Quest]], released in {{ver|14.0}}. The {{Faction|Tenno}} must decipher cryptic poems and solve riddles to locate the {{WF|Mirage}} [[Warframe]].
==Walkthrough==
{{Spoiler|Please finish the quest before proceeding.}}
In order to unlock this quest, the player must complete the [[Eris]] to [[Sedna]] [[Junction]]. Upon completion, the player will be awarded with the Hidden Messages Quest, which can be started from the [[Codex]].

===Riddle One===
Upon starting the quest, [[Ordis]] delivers an inbox message to the player, reciting an inscribed riddle:

{{Quote|Three parts, three acts, three riddles for thee &ndash;<br />
to revive the one wielding fantasy<br />
Ancient gods so cruel, once ruled from on high<br />
Can you name their peak where the land meets the sky?}}

{{CustomCollapsible|Riddle One Answer|RiddleOne}}
The answer to this riddle is '''[[Olympus]], [[Mars]]'''. In Greek Mythology, [[wikipedia:Mount Olympus|Mount Olympus]], the highest mountain in Greece, was considered as the only place where the land scrapes the sky &ndash; At the same time, Mount Olympus is known as the home of the twelve Olympian gods of the ancient Greek world. Olympus Mons, which is located on Mars in real life, is also the tallest mountain in the solar system.

Olympus on Mars is an [[Exterminate]] mission using the [[Infested Ship]] tileset, with {{Faction|Infested}} enemies around level 30.
{{CustomCollapsible/End}}

During the mission corresponding to this riddle, the [[Lotus]] receives cryptic transmissions about a Warframe fighting {{Faction|Sentient|Sentients}} during [[The Old War]], undeterred by the overwhelming odds in spite of the Lotus's orders to retreat.

After completing the mission, the player will receive the '''Mirage Neuroptics Blueprint'''.

===Riddle Two===
[[Ordis]] discovers another transcription alongside the Neuroptics blueprint:

{{Quote|To build the one you think witty,<br />
seek the nymph who sang oh so pretty.<br />
She lured him in with her song and grin,<br />
his wife must've thought it a pity.}}

{{CustomCollapsible|Riddle Two Answer|RiddleTwo}}
'''[[Calypso]], [[Saturn]]'''. In Greek Mythology, [[wikipedia:Calypso (mythology)|Calypso]] was a nymph who is popularly remembered for her role in Homer's epic poem, Odyssey. It is said that Calypso enchanted her singing to trap the fabled Greek hero Odysseus in her island and make him her immortal husband &ndash; forcing Odysseus to be separated from his wife, Penelope.

Calypso on Saturn is a 15-minute [[Survival]] mission set in an [[Infested Ship]], with more [[Infested]] enemies of level 28-35.
{{CustomCollapsible/End}}

The Lotus receives more cryptic transmissions where the Warframe has been captured by the enemy, unable to be saved.

The mission rewards the '''Mirage Systems Blueprint'''.

===Riddle Three===
The Systems blueprint reveals one final riddle:

{{Quote|One more act before your prize is caught.<br />
An ancient sea creature, take a whirl or not?<br />
Look for the monster that swallowed sailors of yore.<br />
Make a mistake and you're sunk. Nothing more.}}

{{CustomCollapsible|Riddle Three Answer|RiddleThree}}
'''[[Charybdis]], [[Sedna]]'''. In Greek Mythology, [[wikipedia:Charybdis|Charybdis]] was a sea monster, later rationalized as a whirlpool and considered a shipping hazard in Strait of Messina. It is said that three times a day, Charybdis swallowed a huge amount of water, before belching it back out again, creating large whirlpools capable of dragging a ship or even a galleon underwater.

Charybdis on Sedna is a [[Hive Sabotage]], with enemies of level 30-40.
{{CustomCollapsible/End}}

The Lotus receives the last of the components, the '''Mirage Chassis Blueprint''', as Mirage tells the Lotus not to despair before she is disintegrated by the enemy.

With the final component in hand, Ordis reads out the last transcription:

{{Quote|Three acts complete, the end draws near,<br/>
soon Mirage will cause fear.<br/>
Memory lost, to be reborn,<br/>
a new warrior rises, duty sworn.}}

The quest is considered completed and player can start building {{WF|Mirage}} with her blueprint from the [[Market]].

